message: "If you use the Spatial Kernel in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Spatial Kernel: deterministic two-view verification of robot task outcomes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
url: https://www.parallaxmetrology.com/spatial_pm.html
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/spatial-kernel
keywords: [robotics, embodied AI, success detection, VLM evaluation, stereo parallax, verification]
abstract: >
  A deterministic check of robot task outcomes: task-region geometry plus a
  two-view parallax test on ordinary photos that separates real 3D objects from
  flat printed decoys. On real phone photos, Gemini Robotics-ER passed 10 of 18
  flat decoys as real objects; the two-view check caught all 10.
